  "worked_solution": "First, note that\n\n$$\n\u00ac(X\u2228Y)\u21d2Y\u2261\u00ac(\u00ac(X\u2228Y))\u2228Y.\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negations, we reach\n\n$$\n\u00ac(\u00ac(X\u2228Y))\u2228Y\u2261(X\u2228Y)\u2228Y.\n$$\n\nFinally, by the associative and idempotent law, we have\n\n$$\n(X\u2228Y)\u2228Y\u2261X\u2228Y.\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $X\u2228Y.$",
